53
00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:17.600
point. Containers can run baseline and
candidate side by side

54
00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:24.133
with a controlled route switch. A cluster
can use a

55
00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:30.667
rolling update, bounded canary, or
blue-green service. A shadow comparison

56
00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:37.200
can observe candidate behavior only when
it cannot create user-visible

57
00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:43.733
or external effects and its data use is
approved. Kubernetes

58
00:05:43.733 --> 00:05:50.267
Deployments support declarative rollout
and rollback mechanics, but the

59
00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:56.800
application still owns exact model
identity, quality gates, mixed-version

60
00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:03.333
behavior, and state compatibility. Define
maximum users or traffic, observation

61
00:06:03.333 --> 00:06:09.867
window, success and guardrail indicators,
cost ceiling, required approver, and

62
00:06:09.867 --> 00:06:16.400
automatic or manual stop conditions.
Verify artifact identity, readiness,

63
00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:22.933
warm-up, policy, telemetry, and rollback
availability before exposure. Drain old

64
00:06:22.933 --> 00:06:29.467
