66
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.800
Checkpoint. A newer candidate improves
average quality, but it fails

67
00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:47.600
one predeclared safety gate and breaks a
required client behavior

68
00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:53.400
during the canary. The model name is newer
and the

69
00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:59.200
rollout has used only five percent of
traffic. What happens

70
00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:05.000
