71
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:25.889
Stop the rollout. Five-percent exposure
limits blast radius; it does

72
00:08:25.889 --> 00:08:31.778
not convert a hard failure into an
acceptable result. Preserve

73
00:08:31.778 --> 00:08:37.667
candidate and baseline identities, exact
routed requests, the safety failure,

74
00:08:37.667 --> 00:08:43.556
compatibility trace, decision, and any
affected state without copying unnecessary

75
00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:49.444
content. Remove candidate traffic, verify
the approved baseline, reconcile in-flight

76
00:08:49.444 --> 00:08:55.333
work, and issue a hold or reject
disposition. A revised

77
00:08:55.333 --> 00:09:01.222
candidate must return through the
qualification gates. If your answer

78
00:09:01.222 --> 00:09:07.111
continued because the model is newer or
the average improved,

79
00:09:07.111 --> 00:09:13.000
restore the authority of predeclared
safety and compatibility gates.

80
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:19.867
Treat rollback as a tested release of the
complete known-good

81
00:09:19.867 --> 00:09:26.733
unit. Retain model, tokenizer, runtime,
image, adapters, prompt and safety

82
00:09:26.733 --> 00:09:33.600
policy, infrastructure configuration,
secret references, telemetry contract, and

83
00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:40.467
deployment procedure. Identify state that
may have changed during the

84
00:09:40.467 --> 00:09:47.333
candidate: database schemas, queue
formats, caches, tool side effects,

85
00:09:47.333 --> 00:09:54.200
evaluation records, or user-visible work.
For every forward-only change, provide

86
00:09:54.200 --> 00:10:01.067
a compatible reader, restore procedure,
migration reversal, or documented

87
00:10:01.067 --> 00:10:07.933
compensating path. Rehearse rollback
before production using the same

88
00:10:07.933 --> 00:10:14.800
